# Agentic Reasoning Guardrails

**Trigger**: Always active. These guardrails correct well-documented reasoning failure modes that affect coding agents across models.

## Why This Rule Exists

LLM-based coding agents exhibit reproducible reasoning failures. These guardrails enforce correct behavior regardless of the underlying model.

| Failure Mode | Symptoms | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **Tool loop amplification** | Near-duplicate reasoning across many turns, one tiny tool call per turn | Wastes tokens, degrades quality, burns context |
| **Phantom tool calls** | Plans tools in reasoning but never executes them; fabricates results | Incorrect code, missed verification, wasted turns |
| **Tool hallucination** | Invents non-existent tool function names | Calls fail silently or produce garbage |
| **Context bloat** | Reads entire files when snippets would suffice; loads generated/lock files | Premature context compression, lost relevant context |
| **Serial drip-feeding** | One file read per turn across 10+ turns instead of batching | 10x+ turns for tasks that should take 2-3 |

Sources: [qwen-code #2863](https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/issues/2863), [opencode #22142](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/22142), [Qwen3 #1817](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3/issues/1817), [Qwen3.6 #15](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3.6/issues/15), [qwen-code #4089](https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/issues/4089)

